tate":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-10-13T19:42:48Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T19:55:27Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.7.2\n\n### System information\n\nWin 10\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen renaming a node and dragging selected text out of the Scene dock bounds, you get stuck in a drag state. This can cause your cursor to get stuck displaying a resize or stop icon sometimes but moving the cursor to an edge of *any* of the `ScrollContainers` in editor to scroll as if you're dragging an element within it as seen with the `Inspector` dock in the gif below.\n\n<img width=\"558\" height=\"345\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/727582a5-4076-4a5d-b14e-400e1befd1cf\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Rename a node in the Scene dock.\n2. Drag the selected text/name with your mouse to right until out of the Scene dock.\nThis will exit out of the rename `PopupPanel`but will get you stuck in the `PopupPanels` drag state.\n\n_You can exit out of it by renaming any node, select the text and hitting the Esc key. When stuck in the drag state, renaming and clicking outside of the `PopupPanel` to exit out of the renaming `PopupPanel`doesn't work, only by hitting the Esc key._\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124445/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124445/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}